# PROBE union. A ⊑ B ⊔ C with B ⊑ D and C ⊑ D entails A ⊑ D, which needs reasoning by cases.
# construct: ObjectUnionOf
# expect: sub :A :D
# expect-not: sub :A :B

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:B rdfs:subClassOf :D .
:C rdfs:subClassOf :D .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ; owl:unionOf ( :B :C ) ] .
